From: AllyncID <177745969+AllyncID@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Wake machines accessed through live Paper block states

Conservative wake-up for snapshot-disabled BlockState access, including timer
setters that mutate native fields directly. Ordinary detached snapshots stay
separate until native update/load applies them. Depends on Minecraft 0041.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/block/CraftBlockEntityState.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/block/CraftBlockEntityState.java
index 1ef1943c9..a4ce46de5 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/block/CraftBlockEntityState.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/block/CraftBlockEntityState.java
@@ -124,4 +124,5 @@ public abstract class CraftBlockEntityState<T extends BlockEntity> extends Craft
     // gets the cloned BlockEntity which is used to store the captured data
     protected T getSnapshot() {
+        if (this.snapshotDisabled && this.snapshot != null) this.snapshot.quantumWake(); // Quantum - live BlockState setters can mutate timers directly
         return this.snapshot;
     }
